+
+## Canic external-contract closeout exports
+
+The management feature additionally exposes the existing pinned 0.11.0 lifecycle,
+settings, ECDSA and complete change-origin/record identities needed by Canic's
+external adapters. These are explicit upstream types, not new call workflows,
+cryptographic implementations or execution authority. Canic's uninstall request
+with sender version maps to UninstallCodeArgs, not the ordinary CanisterIdRecord.
+
+The ledger feature additionally exposes TransferArg and Memo. Its explicit
+icrc21 namespace exposes consent request, metadata, display, response and error
+DTOs; icrc21::Value remains distinct from the existing generic ledger Value.
+There are no blanket upstream module exports or compatibility aliases.
+
+Consumer adoption requires a published supplying version. Full CanisterSettings
+has optional fields absent from Canic's subset, and CanisterInstallMode has the
+complete external variant set. Re-encode new operations, measure their actual
+request cost and preserve original encoded bytes across uncertain retries. Do
+not assume the prior local subset emitted byte-identical Candid type tables.
+Canic still owns endpoint authorization, controller/caller/version bindings,
+reply admission, allowed actions, paid-effect ordering and same-release recovery.
+
+CMC, Cycles Ledger creation, NNS and asset DTO families are not supplied by this
+export addition. They require separately identified canonical suppliers. No
+Canic dependency adoption or published-version availability is asserted here.
